# What must never reach the build context.
#
# Two reasons, and the first one matters more: anything copied in is readable in
# the image and in its layer history, even if a later step deletes it. The
# editor password lives in .env, so that stays out — it is passed to the running
# container instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
.github

# Rebuilt inside the image. Copying a local build in would ship whatever state
# this machine happened to be in.
node_modules
dist
.vite

# Raw asset sources — around 80MB of downloads and archives. The pipeline's
# output is committed under public/assets, so the image does not need these, and
# optimize-assets handles their absence by finding nothing to do.
3dassets
Nieuwe modellen

# Local runtime state. Scores and levels belong on a volume, not in the image.
data

.claude
.idea
.vscode
*.log
.DS_Store
